#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/15-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:831
msgid "Unlike NumPy ([session 14](./14-numpy-pandas-intro.md#missing-values-in-numpy-nan)), pandas skips `NaN` in `sum`, `mean`, `min`, `max` - like SQL and SAS `PROC MEANS`:"
msgstr ""

#. box title
#: site/lectures/15-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:844
msgid "A mean that skips is a different mean"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/15-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:845
msgid "`mean()` divides by the values that are there (398 here), not by all rows. If a missing amount means 0, fill it first - that changes the mean. Decide what a missing value means before you aggregate."
msgstr ""

