#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/15-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:897
msgid "NaN in comparisons, groups and joins"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/15-pandas-select-aggregate-join.md:909
msgid "`!=` is `True` for `NaN` (SQL would give `NULL`, and drop the row); `groupby` drops the `NaN` key unless `dropna=False`. In `merge`, `NaN` keys **match each other** - unlike SQL, where `NULL = NULL` is not true:"
